  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given 222 integers AAA and BBB.\n\nFind any integer XXX (0≤X&lt;2300 \\leq X \\lt 2^{30}0≤X&lt;230) such that ∣(A⊕X)−(B⊕X)∣| (A \\oplus X) - (B \\oplus X) |∣(A⊕X)−(B⊕X)∣ is **minimized**.\n\nHere, ⊕\\oplus⊕ denotes the bitwise XOR operation, and ∣A∣|A|∣A∣ denotes the absolute value of AAA.\n\nIf there are multiple possible XXX that minimize the given expression, you may print any of them.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line of each test case will contain two space-separated integers AAA and BBB.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the integer XXX (0≤X&lt;2300 \\leq X \\lt 2^{30}0≤X&lt;230) that minimizes the given expression.\n\nIf there are multiple possible answers, you may print any of them.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "0≤A,B&lt;2300 \\leq A, B \\lt 2^{30}0≤A,B&lt;230"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n1 2\n3 3\n5 1\n0 15",
        "output": "4\n0\n11\n8",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: ∣(4⊕1)−(4⊕2)∣=∣5−6∣=1| (4 \\oplus 1) - (4 \\oplus 2) | = | 5 - 6 | = 1 ∣(4⊕1)−(4⊕2)∣=∣5−6∣=1.\nIt can be shown that difference cannot become less than 111.\nNote that there are multiple possible answers here: for example X=0X = 0X=0 or X=3X = 3X=3 would also be acceptable.\nTest case 222: ∣(3⊕0)−(3⊕0)∣=∣3−3∣=0| (3 \\oplus 0) - (3 \\oplus 0) | = | 3 - 3 | = 0 ∣(3⊕0)−(3⊕0)∣=∣3−3∣=0, which is the minimum possible difference.\nTest case 333: ∣(5⊕11)−(1⊕11)∣=∣14−10∣=4| (5 \\oplus 11) - (1 \\oplus 11) | = | 14 - 10 | = 4 ∣(5⊕11)−(1⊕11)∣=∣14−10∣=4, which is the best we can do.\nTest case 444: ∣(0⊕8)−(15⊕8)∣=∣8−7∣=1| (0 \\oplus 8) - (15\\oplus 8) | = |8 - 7| = 1∣(0⊕8)−(15⊕8)∣=∣8−7∣=1."
      }
    ]
  },
